# Merge behaviour for the coordination logs two campaigns append to at once.
#
# Minted 2026-09-21, after ralph/DECISIONS.md conflicted for the fourth time on
# one cause: parallel campaigns append to the end of a single file, so every
# merge collides on text neither side disagrees about (see the appendix entries
# for dm-misnamed-coverage and dm-next-edit-move, and the A69-A75 renumber).

# ralph/DECISIONS.md is GENERATED from ralph/decisions/ by
# scripts/ralph-decisions.py. The entry files are one-per-decision and merge
# cleanly on their own, so the render holds nothing the merge needs: keep
# either side and re-render afterwards. `ralph-generated` is a driver, not a
# built-in — scripts/install-git-hooks.sh registers it as `true` (git's own
# recipe for a keep-ours driver). An unregistered clone falls back to the
# ordinary text merge with a warning, which is exactly today's behaviour, so
# nothing is silently worse. What makes keep-ours safe is the ratchet:
# `ralph-decisions.py --check` runs in scripts/pre-push.sh, so a render that
# is missing the other side's entries cannot be pushed.
ralph/DECISIONS.md merge=ralph-generated

# ralph/REVIEW_FINDINGS.md is append-only prose with no ids to collide, so
# union is the correct resolution rather than a convenient one: both campaigns'
# sections land in full, with no markers. Union's own failure mode — an edit to
# an existing line landing twice — is visible on the page, which is not true of
# a numbered ledger, and is why DECISIONS.md is handled differently above.
ralph/REVIEW_FINDINGS.md merge=union
